<p>
	<strong>How we examine planning applications</strong>
</p>
<p>An Inspector or appointed person examines the application and makes the final decision.</p>
<p>They will decide whether to examine the application using one of two procedure types:</p>
<ul>
	<li><strong>written representations</strong> (reviewing written comments and supporting attachments)</li>
	<li><strong>hearing</strong> (a meeting led by the Inspector or appointed person)</li>
</ul>
<p>We will notify you about the chosen procedure if you are:</p>
<ul>
	<li>the applicant</li>
	<li>the local planning authority</li>
	<li>anyone who submitted a comment</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Changes to the process</strong></p>
<p>
	We can change how an application is examined at any time before making a final decision.
</p>
